 ## Operating characteristics
-**Time Complexity:** The guidance field evaluation is efficient using kd-tree queries, avoiding the need to splat values into a regular grid [S1]. Culling typically removes a large percentage of sample points, significantly reducing memory and query time [S1]. Table 1 in [S1] shows that culling can reduce running time from ~27 minutes to ~7 minutes for a large dataset, despite the overhead of culling.
+**Time Complexity:** The guidance field evaluation is efficient using kd-tree queries, avoiding the need to splat values into a regular grid [S1]. Culling typically removes a large percentage of sample points, significantly reducing memory and query time [S1]. Table 1 in [S1] shows that culling can reduce running time from ~27 minutes to ~7 minutes for a large dataset, despite the overhead of culling [S1].
 **Memory Complexity:** Reduced significantly by culling unnecessary samples [S1].
 **Strengths:** Robust front interference tests proven by guidance field properties; prevents sharp changes in triangle size; bounds Hausdorff distance and aspect ratio; no need for regular grid splatting [S1].
